; An effect's name, or `handle`, where a value goes. Each checked OK and
; emitted a register or a symbol nothing defines - `%IO`, `@Console`,
; `%handle` - which llc refused (tests/fuzz/builtin-name-value.axfuzz,
; found by the seeded fuzzer 2026-09-27). They were quiet because a
; `handle` list used to be parsed as an APPLICATION and put each effect
; name where an argument goes; `handle` has been its own form since, and
; its effect list is never read as variables.
;
; Now each is the AX3001 the sixth built-in effect `Unsafe`, and the
; keywords `if`, `let` and `match`, always drew. The `handle` form at the
; end still names `Console` in its list, and draws nothing.
(effect Console
  (say :: (-> Int Int)))

(:: g (-> Int Int))
(fn (g x)
  x)

(:: asValue Int)
(fn (asValue)
  (g IO))

(:: asHead Int)
(fn (asHead)
  (Console 1))

(:: keyword Int)
(fn (keyword)
  (g handle))

(:: main Int)
(fn (main)
  (handle (say 1) (Console) (lambda (n) n)))
